q('How should maintenance lactulose usually be titrated for overt HE prevention?', 'Toward about two to three soft bowel movements daily while avoiding diarrhea and dehydration',[
 ('Until ten watery stools occur every day','Overtreatment can cause dehydration and electrolyte problems that worsen HE risk.'),('Until ammonia is zero regardless of stool effects','A laboratory target does not replace clinical titration.'),('Only once weekly regardless of bowel response','This is not an effective response-based maintenance strategy.')],
 'Use stool quality and frequency without provoking a new precipitant', '**Lactulose reduces intestinal ammonia generation/absorption through several mechanisms.**', ['The 2026 guideline also emphasizes stool characteristics rather than frequency alone.','Severe acute episodes can need a different initial administration strategy.'], '**Review adherence and tolerability before calling treatment ineffective.**', ['Excess diarrhea is a reason to adjust, not a sign of ideal dosing.','Hydration, sodium and potassium should be considered.'], [['Goal','2–3 soft stools/day'],['Too much','Diarrhea/dehydration risk'],['Follow-up','Clinical state and bowel pattern']], [HE])
